            "review_title": "Review at Chi Mac Korea",
            "review_text": "LotusLiLi\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam227 contributions\n0\nAwesome crispy fried chicken\nAug 2017 • Business\nKoreans really know how to make good chicken.\nI don’t like Korean food generally, but this place knows chicken. Way better than KFC.\nI was scared of getting sick from seafood, so I went for the safe bet- Chicken and Beer, you can’t go wrong.\nWe eat fried chicken in Saigon, but the best I’ve had was here at Chi Mac\n\nThere's lots of side dishes they throw in for free too, like some Korean style pickles, rice, and some salad.\nThere was some Korean soups, and noodles too on the menu, but I just came for the chicken.\nThere was a few locals and tourists eating. An American couple we got chatting to \nsaid it was the best chicken they’ve had outside U.S.\n\nI tried the plain fried crispy chicken with just fresh lemon salt and pepper, this was my favourite- and surprisingly not too greasy.\nThe other chicken dish, which I downed easily was the sweet and sour chicken.\nI 'm looking forward to smashin some more next month when we return.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten December 13, 2017",
